WEBVTT

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:05.940
We are now checking in candidates who wish to give a speech.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:10.070
Those interested should come to the EAC office located below the stage.

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:12.560
Yuuki, you're up.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.420
But I don't have the script yet.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:15.620
Yuu-kun!

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:19.950
Sorry I took so long.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:26.710
Far be it from me to stop you.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:30.840
You should follow the path that you believe in.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:36.280
However, you might find yourself at a dead end.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:41.100
Should that happen, I'll be there to guide you.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:50.190
Th-This is the script for the speech!

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.990
That means I gave Yuu-kun the...

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:34.880
Only a few Oojima Rolls left!

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.140
Only a few more copies of our latest book are left!
What do I do? What do I do?

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:38.820
The same goes for our garage kits!
What do I do? What do I do?

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.890
Please support Oojima.
What do I do? What do I do?

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.190
What do I do? What do I do?

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:46.140
Kiba-senpai, what's wrong?

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.400
She's just nervous.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.240
The speech she wrote is about to be read aloud in public, after all.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.620
It'll go great! There's nothing to worry about!

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.080
I'm sure you did a perfect job as usual!

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.780
That's not what I'm worried about.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:01.700
I need to get this to Yuu-kun!

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:02.090
Independent
Independent
Oojima Yuuki
Oojima Yuuki

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:05.000
Oojima Yuuki will begin his speech shortly.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:05.940
What?

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.500
Mifuyu?

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.320
Already? I didn't even get to review—

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:15.700
Pardon us.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.510
Tatsumi Moheiji will deliver his speech next.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:22.600
D-Don't surprise me like that.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:32.180
Thank you, thank you!

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:35.770
I am Tatsumi Moheiji, the candidate endorsed by the General Affairs Commission.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.530
That's some boisterous cheering.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.520
As you're all aware,

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:46.460
the rule of the Public Safety Commission will be coming to an end this term.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:49.660
It is very important that you do not choose the wrong successor.

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:55.080
You see, everyone, there is a great deal of frivolous spending in the current academy budget.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.080
In particular,

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:59.260
the Public Safety Commission, the group responsible for the disgraceful Oosawa Incident,

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.670
holds a plethora of unaccounted expenditures.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:06.880
If you elect me as Student Council President, I'll examine every detail of the budget

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:08.680
and cut all the frivolities!

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:12.190
There might be a certain other
candidate who makes the same promise.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:14.260
However, I urge you to consider the following:

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:17.700
Who is the person who planned that budget?

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.940
<i>He's attacking Shinonome-san!</i>

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.980
While the President makes the final approval,

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:27.180
was there ever a dispute regarding the budget?

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:30.500
Did they ever oppose the President's decisions?

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:31.360
Never!

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.370
Exactly!

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:36.200
The Finance Commission, which blindly passed shady budgets,

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.130
has no right to criticize the current administration!

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:41.380
You can say that again!
You're the man for the job!

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.630
He even planted sympathizers?!

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:46.560
Thank you for you listening.

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:52.220
Please give your vote to the candid candidate, Tatsumi Moheiji.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:58.880
Oh, right. I don't have time to listen to other speeches.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.000
Ms. Shinonome Satsuki, you're on next.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:01.580
Yes.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:02.030
Huh?

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:04.400
Shinonome-san...

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:10.280
Let's both do our best.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:12.540
Yeah, let's.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:18.040
Next a speech from the candidate endorsed by the Finance Commission,

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.040
Shinonome Satsuki.

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:35.060
I am Shinonome Satsuki, the candidate endorsed by the Finance Commission.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:40.060
Satsuki!

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:43.680
Hey, you're back.

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:45.160
Are you feeling okay, Mifuyu?

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:46.540
I...

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:49.800
What happened to Yuu-kun's speech?

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:50.740
He hasn't given it yet.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.580
Mifuyu? What's wrong, Mifuyu?

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:56.940
At a glance,

00:05:56.940 --> 00:06:01.590
the numbers may seem to suggest that the Student Council's budget is in good condition.

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:07.840
But the truth is that both the receipts and expenditures are extremely unbalanced right now.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.620
The reason for these inconsistencies can be attributed to

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:17.350
the gradual, systematic changes in Student Council operations.

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:19.400
She's got a big mouth.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.820
How scary.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:27.000
Not only does she have wonderful and genuine policies
that consider both the school and student body,

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.490
she has the looks and popularity to match.

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:32.700
Her straightforward personality makes her words even more convincing.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:38.040
However, isn't it a shame that such straightforwardness could also work against her?

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:43.720
My mistake! I forgot we were still rivals, Mr. Oojima.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:59.460
Yes, to maintain this high degree of autonomy in the long run,

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:01.650
revolutionary changes need to be made.

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:03.700
We can't afford to stay as we are.

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:07.150
I need to focus on my own speech!

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:12.720
"This wish is closest to my heart."

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:18.460
"I know it will never come true,
but I can at least dream that it will."

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:21.290
Huh? Was this the speech?

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.790
Yuu-kun, wait for me!

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:27.550
I am determined to make bold changes!

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.850
<i>"Yuu-kun, you have someone important to you."</i>

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:32.550
<i>"You have Chisato."</i>

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:35.300
Though they may cause me pain, I will not stop.

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:40.600
<i>"Nothing could make me happier than to see you two happy."</i>

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:44.060
<i>"But let me say it just once."</i>

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:45.560
Please, everyone!

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:46.860
<i>"Just this once."</i>

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:49.570
Lend me your support!

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:52.660
<i>"I... Yuu-kun, I..."</i>

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:56.080
<i>"I love you!"</i>

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:05.790
What is this?

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:08.600
The script for the speech sounds almost like...

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:12.090
a love letter from Mii-chan!

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:14.620
How stressed out <i>am</i> I?

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:18.240
Next, a speech from Oojima Yuuki,
an independent candidate.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:21.680
Please prepare to go on, Mr. Oojima.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:22.730
O-Okay!

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:27.150
I didn't get to review it in the end.

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:30.650
I'll have to read it off...

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:36.380
Wait! Wait, Yuu-kun!

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:37.740
Who are you?

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:39.200
Please, let me through!

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.240
We can't!

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:46.120
It's time.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:50.640
Wait!

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.030
Oh, come <i>on</i>!

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:57.400
People, you're supposed to laugh!

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:03.500
My name's Oojima Yuuki!

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:05.700
It's Oojima, not Ooshima!

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:08.320
It's Jima! Make sure you get it right!

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:10.460
Otherwise, your vote won't count!

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:13.710
I have just one thing to tell you guys today!

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:17.590
Elect me, and I'll put an end to the club reform measures!

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:20.300
A whole bunch of clubs are facing budget cuts,

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:22.510
while others face reorganization and mergers!

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:27.270
As a matter of fact, the Food Club I'm in is gonna get disbanded!

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:32.100
I'll do anything I can to stop it from getting disbanded!

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:34.660
I'm sure you're all in the same boat, so please...

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:35.780
give me...

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:38.030
your votes!

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:44.260
Good! Now that we're all friends,

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:47.540
let me tell you a secret that I'd only tell my friends!

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:50.540
I call it the Seven Food Club Vows!

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:53.000
Let's go! First!

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.420
First!

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:05.060
The polls will close shortly.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:08.560
If you have not cast your vote, we ask that you do so promptly.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.400
Now I've done it.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:11.560
I suck!

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.980
Would you stop that?

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:16.070
We keep telling you that you did just fine!

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:19.900
But I don't remember what happened at all.

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:21.820
The reception was pretty positive.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.380
Non-chan was moved, too!

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:27.240
You were so cool that I almost came.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:31.060
Who knew you'd start talking about the Seven Food Club Vows, then jump to the origins of the universe,

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:33.860
and then to the history of <i>youkan</i>?

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:35.920
Who knew it started from a lamb dish?

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:38.340
What the hell did I talk about?

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.860
You may not remember what you said,

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:45.060
but I'm sure everyone who heard it will never forget.

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:45.760
You think so?

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:48.440
Sorry, Mii-chan.

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:53.020
You went through so much trouble to get me the script, but I was too nervous to read it over

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:54.940
and ended up improvisi—

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:56.480
Don't worry about it.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:59.280
It was far more moving than what I wrote.

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:00.280
Really?

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:03.110
Yes, really! You were amazing, Yuu-kun.

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:05.960
Was I? I'll stop worrying, then.

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:09.620
Excuse me.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:11.740
Huh? Aren't you...

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:15.060
The webcast of the election special is about to begin.

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:17.520
I'll be reporting live from here.

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:18.130
Huh?

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:20.630
Why are you in a boys' uniform today?

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:23.560
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:27.140
I'm a boy, so of course I'd wear a boys' uniform.

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.520
It's a different person?

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:36.180
With whom did you entrust the future of this school?

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:40.530
Good afternoon. I'm your host for this ASP election special, Haratachi.

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:45.030
Earlier today, primaries for the Student Council Presidential Election were held.

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:48.330
With voter turnout
at 98.4 percent,

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:48.520
Votes
Votes
Next Round Qualification

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:48.590
<b>Next Round Qualification
Votes
Votes</b>

00:12:48.590 --> 00:12:52.540
the number of votes to qualify
for the final election is 604.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:52.590
604 votes, huh?
<b>Next Round Qualification</b>

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:54.540
604 votes, huh?

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:57.040
Oh, we already have candidates projected to pass!

00:12:57.650 --> 00:13:01.640
They are the Finance Commission-endorsed candidate, Shinonome Satsuki,

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:04.800
and the General Affairs Commission-endorsed candidate, Tatsumi Moheiji.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.780
They're in a different league.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:08.640
There's no Public Safety Commission candidate this year,

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:10.600
so usually this would be it for the primaries.

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:13.810
But this year, Yuuki's in the race, too!

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:19.900
Now we will be introducing some candidates the ASP picked up on.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:22.360
First is the independent candidate Oojima Yuuki.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.280
It's Ooshima!

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.030
His key policy is "name correction."

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:27.950
What?

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:32.240
The message he left for the voters was,
"Don't just skip the rest!"

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:33.740
What did you do?

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:37.420
Well, I tried to give proper answers, but she...

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:38.720
Well, I guess it's <i>he</i> now.

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:40.500
What are you even talking about?

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:46.280
Now reporting live from the Food Club room, Mr. Oojima's campaign office,

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:47.380
Reporter Shiohama!

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:51.250
Yes. I am at Mr. Oojima's campaign office.

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:52.590
Yay!

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:54.810
How is the general mood over there?

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:56.350
Yay, yay!

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:59.940
There were some smiles before the votes began to be counted,

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:02.270
but the mood has turned serious since.

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:06.440
I see. Please follow up if there are any developments.

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:07.560
Understood.

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:12.280
Why are we getting nervous over a webcast?

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:14.660
An update!

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:17.740
100 votes have been counted. That's 1.7 percent of the total votes.

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:20.500
Sacchan has such a huge lead!

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:23.060
Tatsumi is in second, unsurprisingly.

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:25.800
Oojima-senpai, you're in third place right now!

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:28.260
Eight percent of the votes.

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:30.980
It takes ten percent to pass the primaries...

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:32.810
...so he won't make it at this rate!

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:35.060
The counting just started.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.800
They probably haven't even touched the votes from the seniors yet.

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:38.310
But...

00:14:38.650 --> 00:14:43.240
A good chunk of the seniors vote just for kicks since they'll be graduating,

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:45.840
so the votes are spread all over.

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:47.320
It's still too early to tell.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:51.020
This gets updated every 100 votes, right?

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:54.400
That means there will be 60 more updates.

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:56.040
That many?!

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:11.520
Another update came in!

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:13.350
That's the 15th update.

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:18.100
Yuu-chan has 138 votes, which is 9.2 percent of the total votes!

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:21.120
That's 0.1 percent less than last time.

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:24.110
Wait, doesn't fourth place have a higher percentage than before?

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:30.610
Shirakawa Ayame had 8.6 percent last time, but now she has 8.8 percent!

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:33.620
So there <i>was</i> a serious candidate other than Yuu-kun.

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:35.920
She was trying to appeal to voters with claims of being

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:39.080
a real revolutionary not affiliated with the three commissions!

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:42.260
Where her support and votes are coming from is a mystery.

00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:45.880
I investigated the rumors going around, but I couldn't figure out anything.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:51.380
Even if she gathers over ten percent of the votes,
I'm sure you'll be all right, Oojima-senpai!

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:53.420
The thing is, he won't be.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:56.280
It'll be impossible for him to win if a fourth candidate passes the primaries.

00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:57.140
Why's that?

00:15:57.140 --> 00:16:00.640
The swing votes will split between you and her.

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:02.060
If that happens,

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:06.840
there's no chance you'll win against the other two, who have secured groups of voters.

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:08.000
I see.

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:14.600
Another update!

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.200
Oojima Yuuki

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:21.860
Ten percent of the votes! Finally!

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:22.620
Finally.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:25.340
With 94.4 percent of the votes counted,

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:27.880
you have 571 votes.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:31.580
They could announce you as a projected qualifier any minute now!

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:33.820
He'll really pass if this keeps up!

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:35.300
This is crazy!

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:39.640
The minimum pass line is 604 votes, so you only need 33 more votes!

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:41.220
We'll make it!

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:44.900
We got so many more votes since they started counting the seniors' votes!

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:47.440
But we can't relax just yet!

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:49.940
Here.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:54.120
Shirakawa Ayame has 9.8 percent of the votes!

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:59.440
We just got a third projected qualifier!

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:01.830
Candidate Oojima is projected to pass.

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:06.940
He has become a projected qualifier with 97.7 percent of the total votes counted.

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:08.540
It will be the first time in seven years

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:10.120
that a candidate unaffiliated with

00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:12.590
the three commissions has passed!

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:15.720
Now let's connect to the Oojima campaign office.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:17.910
Reporter Shiohama!

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:19.740
How are things looking there?

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:22.940
We had a moment of rejoicing after his projected qualification was announced,

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:27.620
but it was short-lived, and his campaign staff have returned to the computer

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:30.260
to watch for the outcome of the election.

00:17:30.260 --> 00:17:34.190
Does that mean the qualification alone isn't enough for them?

00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:39.840
Yes, it would seem they are waiting to see if a fourth candidate will pass the primaries.

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:44.710
I see. Please keep us updated on any future developments.

00:17:45.070 --> 00:17:48.500
Shirakawa Ayame has 9.9 percent of the votes so far.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:52.590
At this point, it's easier to look at the vote count rather than the percentage.

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:55.040
The vote count is 584!

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:57.120
With the qualification requirement at 604,

00:17:57.120 --> 00:18:02.080
Shirakawa Ayame only needs 20 more votes to make it, too!

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:04.470
How many votes haven't been counted yet?

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:07.230
140 votes left.

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:09.980
20 out of 140 votes, huh?

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:13.730
If it's just 20 votes, it sounds likely that she'll make it.

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:18.520
Jeez, how come we can't celebrate even though I'm projected to qualify?

00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:20.400
An update!

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:23.040
99.3 percent of the votes have been counted!

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:25.830
Ooshima-shi got 608 votes!

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:28.440
That means you're qualified!

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:30.710
You're not just projected!
You're over the requirement!

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:32.520
Let's celebrate!

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:34.920
Or at least I'd like to.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:36.420
We have still have that problem...

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:39.720
That fourth person is still getting votes.

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:44.470
She has 596 votes.
Eight more, and we're goners.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:48.940
It's so suspenseful! We can't be sure until the very end!

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:51.900
I'm going to have an ulcer at this rate.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:35.190
It's the final update!

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:36.190
% votes counted

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:38.690
Shirakawa Ayame received...
% votes counted

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:39.470
Shirakawa Ayame received...

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:40.700
602 votes!

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:43.070
That's 9.9 percent of total votes!

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:44.780
That means...

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:47.620
She didn't qualify!

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.290
Yuuki's the only independent!

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:51.920
We did it!

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:53.380
All right!

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:55.500
Hooray! Hooray!

00:19:55.990 --> 00:19:57.380
Time for some celebratory drinks!

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:58.670
I'm getting drunk tonight!

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:02.050
I still can't believe it!

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:05.180
Th-Th-This is a miracle!

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:07.700
Well, the rumors did say this would happen.

00:20:08.550 --> 00:20:11.140
Oojima, I'm happy for you.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:12.190
Thank you!

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:18.660
What's up?

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:22.340
Garage and I prepared this.

00:20:25.510 --> 00:20:27.030
Is that...

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:31.180
We're donating part of the proceeds from the sales!

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:35.460
We agreed to do this if you passed the primaries.

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:37.540
Mieru! Garage!

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:42.540
Campaigning from now on will take a lot of resources. You'll need all the funds you can get!

00:20:42.540 --> 00:20:46.620
Sorry it's probably nothing compared to the General Affairs and Finance Commissions' funds.

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:48.680
No, don't be sorry!

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:50.560
Thanks so much, you two!

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:54.060
We'll make good use of this money!

00:20:54.530 --> 00:20:58.820
Thank you! I'll work even harder for the final election!

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:00.860
Yeah, you'd better!

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:03.420
Our future depends on it!

00:21:03.420 --> 00:21:07.280
That's right! Don't let what's to come scare you!

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:09.000
You got it!

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:12.480
Then why don't we cheer one more time?

00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:13.620
All together!

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:15.330
Good idea!

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:20.210
All right, in celebration of Oojima Yuuki passing the primaries...

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:28.220
Hooray!

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:28.900
Hooray.

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:30.340
Hooray!

00:21:30.340 --> 00:21:31.120
Hooray.

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:32.820
Hooray!

00:21:37.510 --> 00:21:42.600
President Mouri, fourth place candidate Shirakawa Ayame has been identified.

00:21:42.600 --> 00:21:46.040
It seems she received some of the Public Safety Commission votes.

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:48.820
Yes, it was a sabotage attempt by the Katahira Faction.

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:52.900
They won't let things go my way, will they?

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:58.300
Just to be safe, please put a detail on Oojima's person.

00:21:58.300 --> 00:21:59.000
Yes, sir!

00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:24.530
In the classroom, looking out the window,
kyoushitsu no madobe de nagameru

00:22:24.530 --> 00:22:28.490
Watching the sky fade softly into twilight,
yasashii yuugure no sora

00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:32.630
I turn around, and there you are again
furimukeba kimi ga egao de

00:22:32.630 --> 00:22:36.710
Looking at me, you smile
kocchi wo miteta

00:22:36.710 --> 00:22:41.050
"Let's go home," you always say,
issho ni kaerou itsumo no

00:22:41.050 --> 00:22:45.210
Going all the places we go every day
toomawari wo shinagara

00:22:45.300 --> 00:22:49.240
Your fingers are just a step away
mada sukoshi todokanai

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:55.720
But deep inside me, it hurts not holding your hand
yubisaki ga tada setsunakute

00:22:57.350 --> 00:23:02.360
In my heart, I found all these hopes and dreams
ano hi kimi to meguriaeta kara

00:23:02.360 --> 00:23:06.530
Because on that day we happened to meet
takusan no yume wo mitsuketan da

00:23:06.530 --> 00:23:08.720
Even when I wanted to cry,
nakitai toki demo

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:12.420
You always stayed right there by my side
itsumo soba ni ite kurete

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:14.950
I want to thank you so much
doumo arigatou

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:19.210
What I wrote on that page I hid from you
no-to ni kaita himitsu no pe-ji wa

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:23.090
Were the words that I just couldn't say
zutto iezu ni ita kotoba

00:23:23.090 --> 00:23:28.850
Now they float forever as whispers on the wind
ima kaze no naka zutto sasayaku yo nee

00:23:28.850 --> 00:23:36.720
Listen close, it says, "I love you so much"
kiite kimi ga daisuki da yo

00:23:42.490 --> 00:23:44.460
Summer is the season for ghost stories!

00:23:44.460 --> 00:23:46.680
Then let me tell you a scary story.

00:23:46.680 --> 00:23:48.540
It'll take a lot to scare us!

00:23:48.540 --> 00:23:51.880
Starchy carbohydrates are made of glucose molecules stuck together.

00:23:51.880 --> 00:23:53.280
What's so scary about that?

00:23:53.280 --> 00:23:55.700
Udon, which has 100 grams of flour per serving,

00:23:55.700 --> 00:23:58.320
spaghetti, which has 100 grams of flour per serving,

00:23:58.320 --> 00:24:00.710
and soba noodles, which has 100 grams of buckwheat flour per serving,

00:24:00.710 --> 00:24:03.740
all have as many calories as 100 grams of sugar.

00:24:03.740 --> 00:24:04.960
That's scary!

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:07.700
Next time, Episode 7: "Camp!"

00:24:07.700 --> 00:24:11.260
I pray that all those calories go to my boobs! To my boobs!
